From 92be213f889f2852533dba6996c1d38f62e163d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:34:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ActiveAE: the limit of PCM to the display, as a setting

The channels of PCM are limited to what the display declares in its
audio data (its ELD) since "AudioEngine: PCM in no more channels than
the display takes"; the only way to turn that off was
<audio><pcmchannelsfromeld>false</pcmchannelsfromeld></audio> in
advancedsettings.xml. A display that declares less than it takes (a TV
that declares its own 2 channels of PCM, as an LG C5 did on some starts
with its sound bar on eARC, and may pass more to the bar: not known)
then had no way back to the channels of "Number of channels" from the
user interface.

A setting now does it: "Limit PCM channels to what the display
declares" (audiooutput.hadespcmlimit), in System > Audio under "Number
of channels", at the expert level, shown where "Number of channels" is,
on by default: nothing changes until it is turned off. Off, decoded
sound follows "Number of channels" alone, as before that commit; its
help says what that costs where the display does not take them (no
sound with the multichannel tracks that Kodi decodes). The entry of
advancedsettings.xml stays, and either of them off turns the limit off.
The engine takes the change at once (the setting is one of those that
reconfigure it).

The strings are core strings in English (39880, 39881), translated in
Estuary (32110, 32111: es_es, es_ar, es_mx) and shown through
CGUIUtils::GetHadesString().
